This is my first RGRN post :)

After trying my hand at a couple of fast ascensions during last year's
dev/null, I thought I'd have a couple of goes on nethack.eu, a new
fast server nearby that records ttyrecs. I knew what I had to do: my
previous record was set during dev/null at 2:55:58.

My lawful female dwarvish valkyrie started off her adventure without a
pet - rushing far too fast to keep one safe. She quickly dived down
stairs and tried on a helmet she found; suddenly she had a lust for
chaos. After the helmet welded itself to her head she quickly dipped
the helmet in fountains and she saw it glow; as she took it off to
inspect it her mind reverted to lawful, but there were still some
chaotic tendencies in her. She went down as fast as possible killing
all the monsters which stood in the way, finding the oracle. Dipping
her longsword yielded the Excalibur; she felt happy to go on and
crusade against the forces of evil. Having not seen the gnomes of the
mines she went back up; and was repulsed by the evilness of the
dwarves and gnomes. Slaying a few made her feel uneasy however, and
she quickly stopped, thinking that she may have misjudged: however not
before netting herself a nice helm, pickaxe and mithril coat. While
exploring the mines she found a bag which made her stuff feel almost
weightless, and then fell down a hole; climbing back up there was a
watchman and a locked door. Not wanting to anger the watchman she read
a spellbook and memorised fireball; she read it again and got
teleported out into the main town, where she sought down the hardware
shop and bought herself an expensive lamp. After taking a quick stop
off to drop all her items on an altar, she went back to the main
dungeon to search for some gold; for there were more items of value in
the town. After securing sufficient funds and some nice speed boots
from a shopkeeper, she rushed back and bought herself 7 candles, and
another expensive lamp.

She rushed back to the oracle and one story further; finding another
upstairs she dived in, netted herself a wand and some food, and dived
over pits to secure two scrolls, which she marked and bagged. Diving
further while exploring to find downstairs netted her a couple of
wands, scrolls, and potions; and finally she found what she was
looking for: an altar. She dipped all her potions in water to dilute
them, letting their parent identity be lost, and dropped them on an
altar and prayed. Tyr, happy that she hadn't strayed too far from her
true course, was happy to bless her water so she blessed the lamps and
rubbed them, netting herself a silver dragon scale mail and a sceptre
of might. With these secured she went back and massacred a barracks;
she had always fancied herself as a sergeant and a bugle interested
her: but to no avail. All that was netted were some gloves and a wand
of sleep, as well as a bit of food.

She grabbed the pickaxe and, not content with how fast the stairs
were, dug as quickly as possible. Soon she arrived at the castle, and
reading one of those scrolls found in sokoban she tried to attack the
drawbridge with the pickaxe but to no avail. After standing forlorn at
the front of the castle for a while (for she had no striking) she ran
upwards searching for someone to let her in. She met Medusa, but
before she could look at her Medusa had become a statue; and after
pickaxing the statue of Perseus there was a sack and shield of
reflection; but no levitation boots. She went back to the castle,
quaffed some potions then remembered there was a scroll she had found
in a corridor, and decided to try it; suddenly she found herself on
dungeon level 20. She went up exploring the levels for any means of
getting into the castle; she found a shopkeeper, asked that Tyr
forgive her, and attacked him. Netting the wand of striking she
dropped into the castle once more, and zapped the wand at the
drawbridge.

Faced with several soldiers she activated the Sceptre of Might and
with fury and rage attacked; the soldiers never stood a chance.
Ignoring the bugles now she netted a few more wands then headed for a
chest; unlocking it she zapped it but unfortunately nothing happened?
She sensed Tyr had not forgiven her for her earlier crime so she
locked the door and waited for him to forgive her. After about two
thousand turns she decided it was enough and zapped the wand again;
thankful of Tyr this time she wished for a couple of scrolls of
charging; only one was received however. Cursing, she zapped the wand
again, but to no avail; she charged it up and wished for a ring of
levitation, remembering how useless she was without it.

Donning the ring she went to loot the castle storerooms, and killed
orange and blue dragons which she ate; she was now complete with a
full set of resistances (although disintegration was to come later).
Dropping her cloak of displacement she found an opera cloak; she
donned this for the rest of the game, and never identified it.

She dropped into the valley of the dead and had a few fights with
undead before making her way through the mazes of Gehennom. She
dispatched Asmodeus and Juiblex without taking significant damage and
then found the tower of Vlad the Impaler; after netting herself an
amulet of lifesaving and killing a unihorn to take its horn she fought
him to the death and picked up his candelabrum. She left, confused
herself and read a scroll of teleportation; surprised to find herself
in the dungeons of doom she dove into the quest. Donning her ring of
levitation and invoking the sceptre to remove conflict she quickly
cleared the first few levels; finding Lord Surtur she zapped striking
at the drawbridge again to face him; just as she was about to kill him
he teleported away. She found him on the upstairs, waited for him to
come and stole his only means of escape, and won the ensuing fight to
the death.

Grabbing the Orb of Fate and the silver bell she left the quest, never
to return; for now she had become more tainted with evil and did not
want to show it to the quest leader.

She identified her rings and found teleport control; she used it to
return to gehennom, where she found a magic portal. This took her to a
tower which were no match for her sword together with the conflict
surrounding the sceptre of might. She faced the most mighty foe - the
Wizard of Yendor; and despite him going away to heal he was no match
for her steel and he quickly died. Picking up the Book of the Dead she
teleported once again to the bottom of the dungeon. She found a square
that vibrated strangely, and using the lore she had picked up
performed a great invocation, which created stairs leading to the
bottom of hell itself. It was then when she realised she had not
killed Orcus, a mighty demon, and she decided to do so in this great
setting. Teleporting up to him she then brought him down to the depths
of hell itself; but scared he teleported away, perhaps to look for a
greater prize? Making her way back to the stairs (for she had
teleported into the sanctum itself) she found Orcus, and killed him:
picking up the Amulet of Yendor and wand of death must have unleashed
the thought of power in her brain, for she quickly donned the helm of
opposite alignment and began her ascent. The Wizard of Yendor came
back repeatedly trying to steal the Amulet; but her powers of chaos
just finished him off with the wand of death as she climbed. She found
freedom at the top of the dungeon... but no. She got transported to
the plane of earth and had to fight Rodney one last time. Killing him
and his companions she gazed into the Orb of Fate to look for a way
out; but overcome with her chaos she just felt confused. She then felt
greedy but a scroll of gold detection netted her a way out instead of
the gold she desired. Remembering this trick she proceeded to the
portal, digging out a route.

On the plane of air she could not control her movements; this was
quickly fixed by the addition of levitation. She made her way across
the plane, teleporting any air elementals that engulfed her; she could
not understand why there were so many going for her, when everyone
should have been fighting each other. She forgot about this and made
her way to the portal.

On the plane of fire she headed straight for the portal - no fancy
tricks - and almost died. Surrounded she removed a potion of full
healing, quaffed it, then used her extra speed to head away from the
monsters. She then found herself on the plane of water. Levitating
over it her Orb of Fate failed to confuse her, or show her the portal;
she therefore had to guess and went away from the monsters she found
herself near. Ringing the bell of Opening she found many monsters; she
concluded it was cursed and using holy water she removed the helmet
and blessed the bell; for her overpowering lawfulness had come
through, and she was once again to kill the monsters of evil. She
levitated further along, recharged the Bell with a scroll of charging
that she wrote, and found herself right next to the portal; she
thanked Tyr and headed in. Tyr understood her plight and sent her a
guardian angel; but faced with several enemies she decided that to
have them fighting each other was better than fighting only her; and
after she and her angel had dispatched Famine with raw steel she
invoked the Sceptre once again. Tyr rebuked her; this hurt heavily in
her soul, but wishing for another marker she charged her wand of
teleportation and teleported all the monsters away. Heading towards a
high altar she could not deal with the monsters nearby; she teleported
them and accidentally hit the high priest. Making her way into the
temple she took off conflict; but the damage was done. The high priest
paralysed her; and the monsters nearby proceeded to kill her; but the
amulet of lifesaving she was wearing kicked in and she became relieved
and revitalised. She headed straight for the altar, unblinded herself
(for she had become blind with lightning strikes) and saw a high altar
of chaos. Her hurt earlier and her chaotic nature meant she donned the
helm of opposite alignment once more, and offered the Amulet to Loki,
who accepted and granted her demigoddesshood.

Total time: 2h29m13s.

